    {
      "id": "2020-summary",
      "title": "2020 Year in Review",
      "date": "2020.12.30",
      "tags": [
        "Year in Review"
      ],
      "category": "posts",
      "featured": false,
      "excerpt": "",
      "content": "> This post was originally published on my [WeChat public account](https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/wWd5yAbvR2qZDETOJMXC3A).\n> That year I finished the Gaokao and started my university life in Shanghai.\n> *(Added on November 30, 2025)*\n\n---\n\n# January & February\n\nI changed my phone at the beginning of the year, so many photos from January and February were lost.\n\nKind of a pity.\n\n![Snow in February](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130195805.png)\n\nThere was a pretty heavy snowfall sometime in mid-February.\n\n![This one was taken by my mom. Huawei cameras are actually pretty good.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130195820.png)\n\n![It was snowing quite heavily. Also the first time I went downstairs since the pandemic started.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130195913.png)\n\n---\n\n# March\n\nThe most important thing was probably the city-wide mock exam.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/!\\[我和猫猫]\\(\\).png)\n\nMe and the cat.\nI remember this photo very clearly — it was taken before the math exam.\n\nThat time I finished the math paper almost **an hour before the exam ended** (except the insane final problem).\nI confidently told my mom:\n\n> “You can collect the paper. This test is ridiculously easy. No way I score below 140.”\n\n(I was really stupid, honestly.)\n\nMy mom kept telling me:\n\n> “Check your answers!”\n\nAnd guess what — I messed up the multiple choice and fill-in-the-blank probability questions…\n\nThat mock exam score was… not pretty.\n\nAfter the exam, until the next mock exam in Xicheng District, I kept comforting myself every day:\n\n> “Shanghai University isn’t bad either!”\n\nNot long after that something pretty major happened — **the Gaokao was postponed**.\n\nI remember it very clearly: **March 31st, around 11:30 a.m., during history class.**\nSomeone suddenly typed in the meeting chat that the Gaokao had been delayed.\n\nThere were originally **68 days left until the exam** — just over two months. I was basically in despair and had almost given up.\n\nSuddenly it became **97 days**.\n\nI instantly went:\n\n> WOOHOO!!!\n\nNo more browsing Taobao, no more magic tricks, no more messing with cameras.\nIt suddenly felt like I still had a chance.\n\nThank you, Examination Authority, for giving me another chance to start over.\n\nThree years of luck finally kicked in haha.\n\n![Though honestly it wasn't that dramatic. I still occasionally slacked off during sports time.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200017.png)\n\n![Sometimes I'd organize my playing cards when bored.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200037.png)\n\n---\n\n# April\n\n![Every time I opened the door, the cat would lie on the desk. Clearly it didn’t want me studying.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200055.png)\n\n![I always think cats look adorable when they stretch their paws like this.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200125.png)\n\n![Picked up three months’ worth of newspapers. Respect to the delivery guy.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200214.png)\n\nSchool resumed on **April 25th**.\nHonestly I was pretty happy — staring at screens every day was unbearable.\n\n![Three months of hair growth. Probably the longest hair I'll ever have in my life.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200353.png)\n\n---\n\n# May\n\nNothing too special.\n\n![The Will Tsai prop I bought last year finally arrived. Honestly the value was terrible, but TCC threw in a cups-and-balls set worth 800 RMB so it instantly became worth it lol. This prop gave me a lot of inspiration for my graduation performance routine.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200420.png)\n\n---\n\n# June\n\nThe last days of student life.\n\n![Birthday cake. Smelled amazing. The cat clearly wanted some too.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200442.png)\n\nOriginally my birthday was supposed to coincide with **the first day of Gaokao**.\n\nFor many years I had imagined that day:\n**Turning 18 + Gaokao on the same day.**\n\nPretty dramatic.\n\nBut in the end, things changed and I missed that coincidence.\n\nThen on **June 17th**, the **second wave of the pandemic** suddenly hit.\n\nA sudden graduation ceremony announcement exploded everyone's WeChat Moments.\n\n![JoJo pose — my favorite photo. Men's happiness is really this simple.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200513.png)\n\nEven though it was only half a year, it somehow felt like a very long time.\n\nBack home again, suffering through online classes with a painful expression.\n\nI **really hate online classes**.\nThey always give me the feeling that I learned nothing.\n\nSelf-studying and grinding through problems always felt much better.\n\nAbout a week later we heard online classes would last until early July.\n\nMy mentality completely collapsed.\n\nThat night I talked to my homeroom teacher until **10:30 PM**.\n\nThe only thing I clearly remember saying was:\n\n> “If… if my Gaokao results end up being disappointing…\n> I will regret that period of time for the rest of my life.”\n\nLooking back now, I feel both brave and embarrassingly dramatic.\n\nBut I’m truly, truly grateful that **Teacher Li supported my decision.**\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200538.png)\n\n---\n\n# July\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200559.png)\n\nFinally.\n\n![Exam entrance photo]()\n\nThose four days of exams were the **most confident days of my life**.\n(Though I still bombed a few subjects.)\n\nEvery day was just:\n\n* flipping through books\n* petting the cat\n* listening to Beethoven\n\n![Only one subject left — history. But the cat still refused to let me study.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200612.png)\n\nThe most thrilling moment was probably **three minutes before the Chinese exam ended**, when I changed two multiple-choice answers worth three points each.\n\nI kept asking myself:\n\n> “Do you trust yourself or superstition?\n> If you trust yourself, will you regret it?”\n\nSomehow the Chinese exam turned into a psychology test.\n\nLuckily, the answers were correct.\n\n![On the 18th we sent off Huihui. We had taken care of the cat for a year. Hard to say goodbye. At least 15 points of my Gaokao score should be credited to it.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200633.png)\n\n![Bought a Panasonic camera](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200658.png)\n\n![Also bought lots of playing cards…](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200712.png)\n\nA few days after the exams, the graduation ceremony schedule came out, so I started working on a magic routine.\n\nThe creative process was actually very fun.\nThe video format gave me lots of room for creative ideas.\n\nUnfortunately time was limited, and the details weren't as polished as I hoped.\n\n![Originally I wanted to do something crazy and bought a flower pot for experiments. Later realized it was just wishful thinking.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200732.png)\n\nFirst day recording with YSJ — the magic part went smoothly.\n\nBut when recording the speech part, someone suddenly called me on WeChat asking me to go gaming.\n\nI completely lost it.\n\nThe next day we tried recording again — and the upstairs neighbors started drilling.\n\nThe process was… eventful.\n\n![Some people perform magic entirely thanks to lighting](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200753.png)\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200807.png)\n\n[My high school graduation magic performance (2020)](https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1dv411i7jd/?share_source=copy_web&vd_source=2e95f8b32aa6f76a3d42bad6b38256a3)\n\n**Life is Magic.**\n\nI didn't originally plan that line.\n\nBut while looking through my props I found a card I had written who-knows-when.\n\nIt felt appropriate, so I used it.\n\nAfter all, it was a graduation ceremony — being a bit cheesy was acceptable.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200826.png)\n\nThe funny thing was:\n\nGraduation ceremony on the **23rd**,\nScore release on the **25th**.\n\nThose few days were actually pretty fun.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200840.png)\n\nAt **11 PM on the 24th**, I went for a walk with X-brother and we ran into a hedgehog.\n\nWe kept saying:\n\n> “I hope tomorrow at this time I’m still feeling this calm.”\n\nI also remember XDC looking extremely serious and telling me:\n\n> “The score difference between you and me will definitely be within five points.”\n\nI could only respond:\n\n> HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA\n\nWhat an international joke.\n\n![4:30 AM on the 25th. Naturally woke up.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200908.png)\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130200957.png)\n\nVery surreal.\n\nDuring those months I also had many dreams — usually about things like:\n\n* forgetting to fill in the answer sheet\n* writing the English essay off topic\n* scoring 80 in Chinese\n\nEvery time near the end of the dream I'd think:\n\n> “This is too horrible. I must be dreaming. Wake up!”\n\nAnd then I'd wake up.\n\nI’ve never experienced such intense immersion again.\n\n---\n\n# August\n\nDue to pandemic restrictions I stayed in Beijing the entire summer.\n\nEarly in the month I pulled WHR out for an all-night walk.\n\n![2 AM Shichahai](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201056.png)\n\n![4 AM Chang'an Avenue]()\n\n![Probably the lowest traffic of the day](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201135.png)\n\n![6 AM flag-raising ceremony](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201157.png)\n\nSurprisingly there weren’t that many people.\n\nBack then I hadn't taken photography seriously yet.\nI missed many beautiful moments.\n\nHopefully next year when I return to Beijing I can take more photos.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201213.png)\n\nMid-August I received my admission letter.\n\nIt was shipped from Shanghai at **2 PM** and arrived the next day at noon.\n\n**EMS is GOAT.**\n\nA year earlier during a class meeting everyone had to state their dream university.\n\nI said **ECNU Software Engineering**.\n\nOne year later — I actually got in.\n\nSeems my self-assessment was pretty accurate.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201230.png)\n\nECNU even sent a **cherry blossom soap**.\nUsed it once and then stored it away like a luxury item.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201238.png)\n\nWhen the graduation photo arrived I hung it next to the admission letter.\n\nLooking at them together was emotional.\n\nHard to imagine studying in the same place for **12 years**.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201255.png)\n\nAugust 31.\n\nThe last sunset I saw in Beijing.\n\n---\n\n# September\n\nDidn’t go anywhere — just started university.\n\n![High-speed train to Shanghai](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201308.png)\n\nMy parents both came to Shanghai to send me off.\n\nI still feel very guilty.\n\nThat day I was in a bad mood and got irritated while finding seats on the train.\n\nEven now, half a year later, I still feel bad about it.\n\nPeople always become sentimental during farewells.\n\nEventually I moved into the dorm successfully.\n\nI will never forget the first night in the dorm.\n\n**Early September. Shanghai. No air conditioning.**\n\nProbably the closest I’ve ever been to heatstroke.\n\n![Bought a bunch of water on the first day but couldn't carry it upstairs alone. First time realizing the importance of fitness.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201329.png)\n\n---\n\n# October\n\nA month struggling with:\n\n* Calculus\n* Physics\n* Linear Algebra\n\nTurns out my math is **really really really bad**.\n\nNever thought math would become the subject I spend the most time on but do the worst in.\n\nWhen I felt suffocated on weekends I would walk around the streets.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201406.png)\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201415.png)\n\n![Street singer in front of a café](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201424.png)\n\n---\n\n# November\n\nEarly in the month I had dinner with Professor Chen on Nanjing Road.\n\nWhile waiting we walked around the Bund.\n\nCoincidentally we caught the **China International Import Expo light show**.\n\nAlso funny — ECNU software engineering only admits **two students from Beijing**, yet somehow my small district in Shijingshan produced both of them.\n\n![No way someone goes to the Bund without taking the classic skyline photo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201723.png)\n\nMid-month I finished the midterms.\n\nTurns out they weren't as terrifying as expected.\n\nI also performed magic at the freshman welcome party.\n\n[ECNU Software School Magic Performance](https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1SA411j7s6/?share_source=copy_web&vd_source=2e95f8b32aa6f76a3d42bad6b38256a3)\n\nThe last time I stood on a stage before that was probably **middle school graduation**.\n\nI truly enjoyed the cheers and applause that night.\n\nOnly regret was the camera connection failing a few times.\n\n![Thanks to the vice-minister!](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130201837.png)\n\nLater that month I walked around campus after rain.\n\nThe campus has **so many cats**.\n\n---\n\n# December\n\nFirst weekend I went to the **West Bund**.\n\nThe weather had been cloudy for a long time.\n\nIf I had a model to photograph maybe it wouldn’t bother me so much.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130202250.png)\n\nLater I recorded another welcome show.\n\nIt was honestly a **very embarrassing performance**.\n\nI was suddenly told there would be **no headset microphone**, and performing without an audience was much harder than expected.\n\nMy on-stage condition wasn’t great.\n\nA lesson learned.\n\n![Hair gel did its best](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130202303.png)\n\nNear Christmas I visited **Anyi Night Market**.\n\nI probably walked the street **ten times back and forth**.\n\nIf I hadn’t stupidly spent **96 RMB at Shake Shack**, it would've been a perfect night.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130202337.png)\n\nNext day we had a group activity visiting the **Lu Xun Memorial Hall**.\n\nRight next to **Tian’ai Road**, so I visited that famous romantic street as well.\n\n![📮](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130202359.png)\n\nFinally got a sunny weekend.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130202413.png)\n\n![East China Normal University ❌Global Harbor University ✔](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130202450.png)\n\nDecember 30.\n\nThe moon was big, round, and cute.\n\n---\n\n**This year was better and happier than the past few years.**\n\n**I was lucky to finally seize the opportunity.**\n\n**Lucky to enter my dream major at ECNU.**\n\n**Lucky to meet such amazing and fun roommates.**\n\nNext year I hope to:\n\n* travel more places\n* perform more magic\n* take more photos\n* write more code\n* suffer less from calculus\n\nHappy New Year to everyone who read this — and those who didn’t.\n\n![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jiaaming/blogImage/main/pic/20251130202518.png)",
      "locale": "en",
      "sourceLocale": "en",
      "isFallback": false
    }
